    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "With only 7 patients in our rare-disease cohort, I want to see which genes rise and fall together within each individual patient, with a significance value for every gene pair so we can keep the trustworthy links. The expression table is gene-by-sample with a header, log-transformed and centred."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"which genes rise and fall together within each individual patient, with a significance value for every gene pair\" -- available from LIONESS-COEXPRESSION.\n2. \"significance value for every gene pair\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set.\n3. \"With only 7 patients in our rare-disease cohort, I want to see\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set.\n4. \"so we can keep the trustworthy links\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set.\n\nSelected path: **LIONESS-COEXPRESSION**.\n\nYour question asks for a per-sample co-expression network. **LIONESS-COEXPRESSION** fits that result and scale.\n\n**LIONESS-COEXPRESSION** — Infer aggregate and sample-specific co-expression networks with LIONESS. LIONESS represents the cohort network through sample contributions: W_q = N*W_all - (N-1)*W_without_q, where N is the cohort size and the same base estimator is fitted with and without sample q. The leave-one-out network alone is not the patient's network. This borrows cohort information; it does not estimate a correlation from one isolated observation or prove causality. With PANDA, edge weights are inferred regulatory support, not measured binding strength. Cross-sectional networks do not establish temporal rewiring.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `expression_file`: expression matrix\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `coexpression_network`: Inferred gene-to-gene associations.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nInput compatibility has not been assessed: your data was not checked against the workflow's required inputs; name your input files to have them checked. This is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
